# Reverse Singularity Deployment

## Subdomain pattern

`{slug}.reversesingularity.com` — DNS managed on Vercel (domain registrar).

## Vite/React → Vercel

- Build: `npm run build`, output `dist`
- After deploy: alias subdomain to deployment
- **401 on subdomain:** disable SSO protection:
  `vercel project protection disable {project} --sso`
- Monorepo: set Vercel Root Directory (e.g. ALLS uses `mcwi/`)

## Flask/Python → Railway

- Dockerfile + `requirements-prod.txt`; listen on `$PORT` (8080 on Railway)
- Custom domain on Railway → CNAME on Vercel DNS:
  - `{slug}` CNAME → `{id}.up.railway.app`
  - `_railway-verify.{slug}` TXT → `railway-verify=...`
- Do **not** use broken nixpacks-only configs without pip

## Landing page deploy

```bash
vercel link --yes --project reversesingularity_landing
vercel --prod --yes
```

## DNS troubleshooting

If authoritative DNS (8.8.8.8) is correct but local requests hit wrong host, flush Windows DNS cache or use 8.8.8.8 on the adapter.

